{\s17\sa60\sb30\widctlpar\qj \fs22\cgrid 
This function generates an appropriately sized gamma ramp from the specified exponent and then calls {\b glfwSetGammaRamp} with it. The value must be a finite number greater than zero.\par
The software controlled gamma ramp is applied {\i in addition}  to the hardware gamma correction, which today is usually an approximation of sRGB gamma. This means that setting a perfectly linear ramp, or gamma 1.0, will produce the default (usually sRGB-like) behavior.\par
For gamma correct rendering with OpenGL or OpenGL ES, see the {\b GLFW_SRGB_CAPABLE} hint.\par
